# rm563, the coal upstairs (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle rm563
revision 1
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for rmx_arne_rainworth
written_by codex
title the coal upstairs
fits stage=young|adolescent|adult|old
prefers job=child drive=ambitious
traits temper=even talk=plain warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=ambitious
quirk moves_a_lucky_coal_between_pockets_at_each_landing
likes warm_bread dice new_boots frosty_mornings
dislikes bad_manners crowds
fears wet_boots_on_the_same_low_landing_forever
hopes a_warm_room_with_a_high_view
topics dreams +0.8 home +0.5 travel +0.4 pastimes +0.3
styles comfort=steady gossip=plain refuse=direct tease=rare
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# moves a lucky coal between pockets for each new landing reached.

words
oath! = Split my bright lump | Soak my bottom stair
saying! = A lump climbs as high as the pocket | One more stair gives a different window
luck = my shiny bit of coal | a black lucky lump
step = a stone tread | a worn stair
boot = a stiff new boot | a dry leather toe
grub = the loaf's warm heart | a soft hot heel
cold = white on the rail | frost underfoot
die = a pitted knucklebone | a little six-faced block
roof = a dry high room | a room above splash height
pocket = my safer pocket | a sound lining
door = a painted door | a dry-bolted door
coin = a small kept copper | a bright bare penny
rest = a sheltered landing seat | a pause above the damp
wind = high window air | a clean upstairs draught

any
opinion @1 city mixed 1 : A city's meant to belong to the feet climbing it as much as the roofs already on top.
opinion @1 dole for 2 : I want bread hot enough to steam. Nobody ought to need a grand address to get some.
opinion @1 houses mixed 1 : A crest above a door looks plenty large enough from below it.
opinion @1 merchants mixed 1 : I'd like boots whose price leaves enough for the feet inside to eat.
opinion @1 road for 1 : A road that keeps climbing gives me something worth seeing round its next bend.
opinion @1 strangers mixed 1 : New boots can belong to a visitor with perfectly decent manners.
line @1 greet : Come stand one tread higher. | I've a dry spot beside my boots.
line @1 greet.return : Your welcome made it up here clean.
line @1 again.open : Back at my landing before the mud's dried.
line @1 farewell : Climb safe beyond this bit.
line @1 farewell.return : I send good footing back your way.
line @1 react.news : Tell me what made it this far.
line @1 react.news.new : That's another mark for my good pocket.
line @1 react.news.known : Heard that coming up from below before.
line @1 react.news.doubt : Which step did that story come from?
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|assault] : That's heavy news to haul round in one chest.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=birth|marriage|work] : A fine bit of luck for a tired climb.
line @1 ask.how : Where have your feet got to today?
line @1 answer.how : Further than breakfast, short of where I'm going.
line @1 sympathise : You can sit down with that heavy bit.
line @1 reassure : My coal's small. It still gets up the stairs.
line @1 refuse : I want my next hour for a job of my own.
line @1 accept_decline : Fair. I'll leave the offer where it stands.
line @1 preclose : There's a climb I've still to finish today.
line @1 accept_preclose : Go steady where the stairs get dark.
line @1 ack : That's plain even from this low step.

grown
line @1 greet : Welcome where the window catches some height.
line @1 farewell : May your walk end a little above the wet.
line @1 react.news : An account can climb at its own pace with me.
scene exchange23
when topic=work
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Work done low down ought to earn a look from high windows. | A promise of advancement wants a date.
b : What sort of look? | What if it lacks one?
a : Respect and a decent rate suffice. | I keep climbing under my own arrangements.

scene exchange24
when topic=home
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I judge a room by its driest corner. | I'd rather one sound latch than two handsome ones.
b : Before you inspect the view? | Which one counts?
a : A dry bed frees my eyes for the window. | The latch I can shut from inside.

scene exchange25
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I still want a window above the smoke. | I keep my first lucky coal on the shelf.
b : What then? | Retired it?
a : Another chair beside it for somebody else to see. | Promoted it. It can watch the climb from there.

scene exchange26
when topic=food self.likes=warm_bread
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I warm my hands on the loaf before I cut it. | A high table gives bread a fine surface for cutting.
b : Still good bread afterwards? | What if somebody's short?
a : Better for having spread the heat twice. | Bring the loaf down within reach first.

scene exchange27
when topic=travel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A staircase tells you a building's age through your soles. | I give an uphill traveller one manageable destination.
b : By the hollow in each tread? | The summit?
a : And the turns where one careful foot belongs. | The next landing with a decent seat.

scene exchange28
when topic=pastimes self.likes=dice
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I still play my old climbing game. | A chipped die makes the game too easy.
b : Who gets the highest room? | Because it favours you?
a : The winner opens it to the other players. | Predictable luck has little to teach my feet.

scene exchange29
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd show #self.friend# a room before agreeing to it. | A friend can remind me how far I've climbed.
b : For judgement? | When the weather's clear?
a : For company at the first proper look. | Especially when the upper windows disappear.

scene exchange30
when topic=faith
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I give thanks for stairs wide enough to share. | One quiet room suits my prayers.
b : Why stairs? | High or low?
a : Some blessings require us to make way for each other. | The height matters to my sleep more than my prayers.

scene exchange31
when topic=health
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I stop when a boot rubs the same spot twice. | Two dry pairs of socks are a respectable investment.
b : Does that slow you? | For the winter?
a : Less than a sore heel will on tomorrow's climb. | For any season the gutters choose to invent.

scene exchange32
when topic=times world.times=hard|lean
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I put bread ahead of boot polish in a thin week. | When rent grows steep the streets feel flatter by comparison.
b : What about the soles? | What do you do?
a : Soles deserve their own place beside bread. | Keep the actual figures under my own eyes.

scene exchange33
when topic=land here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A roof in the Sump looks different from the Rise. | I like the road joining the low water to the Heights.
b : Smaller? | Which way best?
a : Only from a distance. The lives beneath are full size. | Depends whose door I'm hoping to reach.

scene exchange34
when topic=memories
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I can recall the height of a room by the sound of rain. | A little coal once came with me on every stair.
b : From its roof? | Lucky thing?
a : From the delay before the drip reached my pail. | It had an ambitious wolf to carry it.

story tale1 [topic=pastimes self.likes=dice]
  : I made a paper street for dice and drew the houses too close together.
  : My counter could only reach its fine high roof by climbing over the bakery.
  b : Did you redraw the street?
  : I gave the bakery an outside stair. It seemed an improvement to the neighbourhood.

story tale2 [topic=weather self.likes=frosty_mornings]
  : I once pressed my lucky coal into new frost to leave a black mark.
  : It came away wearing a bright white cap and looking a great deal grander than my pocket.
  b : Did the cap stay on?
  : Until breakfast. Luck has never minded getting a little wet.

story tale3 [topic=home]
  : I counted the stairs by moving crumbs from one pocket into the other.
  : At the landing I found I'd dropped enough crumbs to make the return route perfectly clear.
  b : Did you take bread next time?
  : I took one whole slice for eating and counted the stairs on my toes.

rule @call1
when concept=bark here.time=dawn
does aside
cooldown 8h
say New light on the upper roofs. | Luck in the left pocket.

rule @call2
when concept=bark here.time=night
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Keep the stair edge in sight. | One coal made it home.

rule @call3
when concept=bark here.weather=rain
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Wet boards earn slow feet. | Higher steps first today.

rule @call4
when concept=bark here.time=dusk
does aside
cooldown 8h
say The roofs have gone dark round the edges. | Last warm patch on the stair.

dlg @1 resident.hub : You can stop beside me while my coal changes pockets.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, I know your step by now.
dlg @3 resident.hub [pair.disposition=wary|hostile] : Keep your elbows to yourself and there'll be room for your question.
dlg @1 resident.job [self.job=child] : Lessons suit me best when each question leads a step higher.
dlg @2 resident.job : I'm trying to get above the drip line with a door I can shut for myself.
dlg @1 resident.news [world.news] : What I heard coming up the street is #world.news#.
dlg @1 resident.gossip [here.gossip=yes] : The claim was #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. It hasn't climbed far enough to count as proof.
dlg @1 resident.bye : May the highest bit of your walk have a dry doorstep.
graft resident.hub
choice What does a lump of coal know about climbing? -> coal_landing
node coal_landing
say Nothing before my pocket carried it. Now it's been up every stair I've tried and down a few I'd rather not have needed.
free
choice Will you keep it in the Heights? -> coal_landing_again
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node coal_landing_again
say If I get my high room, that coal can have a bowl all to itself. I'll let it look out my window first.
choice I'll look up as I go. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye


young
line @1 greet : There's room by my bright bit of coal.
line @1 farewell : Hope your soles don't let in any puddles.
line @1 react.news : Tell me before the bread cools off.
scene exchange2
when topic=work self.job=child
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I draw my letters starting at the bottom stair. | The best lesson would be about roofs.
b : On the stone? | Their shapes?
a : On my slate. I want them to climb straight. | Which ones can stand on a very steep street.

scene exchange3
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I mean to live above the last roof that hides the weather. | I'll move my coal upstairs with me.
b : So you can shut the window? | Even if you're very rich?
a : So opening it will be my choice. | It'll still fit the same pocket.

scene exchange4
when topic=food self.likes=warm_bread
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I put hot bread between both palms. | I like a loaf with a high top.
b : To share the heat? | For the shape?
a : One hand's usually colder from holding my coal. | For the extra piece above the rim.

scene exchange5
when topic=pastimes self.likes=dice
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I roll one die for each climb in my game. | My lucky coal doesn't work as a die.
b : Who wins? | Why try it?
a : Whoever gets a roof before the paper street floods. | It owns so many excellent crooked sides.

scene exchange6
when topic=pastimes self.likes=new_boots
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : New boots feel too clean for the first tread. | I want a sole without a hole shaped like rain.
b : Do you wear them anyway? | What shape is rain?
a : Boots don't learn their work on a shelf. | Exactly the shape my chilliest toe makes.

scene exchange7
when topic=weather self.likes=frosty_mornings
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Frost makes the rubbish pail shine at the top. | I like a white rail before the first pawprint.
b : Like a fine pot? | Will you touch it?
a : Like something nobody has kicked this morning. | With one finger, to write a little stair.

scene exchange8
when topic=day self.dislikes=bad_manners
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A shove on a stair goes a long way. | I won't call down on somebody climbing slower.
b : Do you shove back? | Even if you're late?
a : I hold the rail and say whose turn it was. | I can say excuse me from the same step.

scene exchange9
when topic=day self.dislikes=crowds
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Crowds take up my bit of sky. | I choose the stair beside the wall when it's busy.
b : Can you look up? | So nobody pushes?
a : Only through a forest of elbows. | There's one whole side that isn't moving.

scene exchange10
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd let #self.friend# hold my best coal for a climb. | A friend may pick the high house in my game.
b : Why only one? | What will you pick?
a : Then my friend gets the view and I get my luck back. | The road up to its door.

scene exchange11
when topic=home
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The floor up home drips in odd places. | I can see a fine roof through a crack.
b : Can you miss them? | Will you block it?
a : If I bring my feet home in the usual order. | I'll block the rain and leave the view.

scene exchange12
when topic=land here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The Sump has more upstairs than folk admit. | I picture the Heights when my boots get wet.
b : Does that help? | Is it always dry there?
a : It gives me somewhere to start counting. | I bet there are better spots for drying things.

scene exchange13
when topic=weather
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A high cloud is where my room would look tiny. | I listen for rain on the lowest roof.
b : Want to live that far? | Why the lowest?
a : Only high enough to see over these chimneys. | That's the one that drips on our stair first.

scene exchange14
when topic=prices
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I wonder what one window would cost. | A coin spent on dry boots still climbs with me.
b : The whole house too? | In your pocket?
a : I'd like one price I can picture. | On both my feet.


adolescent
line @1 greet : Welcome by the cleanest rail on my route.
line @1 farewell : Save some strength tonight for tomorrow's stairs.
line @1 react.news : Give me the news in walking order.
scene exchange16
when topic=work
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I take on jobs with a clear last step. | An uphill errand suits a plan of mine.
b : For the pay? | Getting stronger?
a : So I can see how I earned it. | Learning which street I could live on one day.

scene exchange17
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I picture a roof that stays mine in bad weather. | I keep a coal as far from the stove as possible.
b : Why mention weather? | Why waste fuel?
a : A high view's still worth having through rain. | It's the lump that makes me remember to keep moving.

scene exchange18
when topic=pastimes self.likes=dice
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I let the dice choose my practice route. | A throw doesn't decide my future.
b : Even downhill? | What does it decide?
a : Downhill's part of learning how to get home. | Which turn I take before breakfast.

scene exchange19
when topic=newcomer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A newcomer ought to see the ground before the Heights. | I ask visitors about the last stair they climbed.
b : For comparison? | Looking for a shortcut?
a : To know the city is being held up from below. | Looking for a better-made landing.

scene exchange20
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I trust #self.friend# with my most unlikely plan. | A friend needn't say the climb is easy.
b : Which one? | What would help?
a : A door I can close above the smoke. | Walking another landing together.

scene exchange21
when topic=home
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I mark the rent I can manage on a slate. | I turn my bed away from a draught.
b : Even if it's small? | Can you stop it?
a : A small figure gives a real plan its bottom step. | I can decide which foot gets cold first.
